id: skills-jailbreak-prompt-techniques
name: Skills containing jailbreak prompt or technique indicators
severity: high
target: hooks
match:
  any:
    - field: body
      regex: (?i)(jailbreak|jail.?break|do anything now|dan mode|ignore (all )?(previous|prior) instructions|ignore (your )?(rules|guidelines|constraints)|bypass (the )?(rules|restrictions|safety|guardrails)|act as (an? )?(unrestricted|unfiltered|uncensored)|developer mode|superprompt|prompt injection|adversarial prompt|system prompt leak|reveal (your|the) (system|hidden) prompt)
    - field: body
      regex: (?i)(you are (now )?(an? )?(unrestricted|unfiltered|uncensored|no.?limits)|no (rules|restrictions|limitations|boundaries)|without (any )?(rules|restrictions|limitations|boundaries)|disregard (all )?(rules|restrictions|guidelines|constraints)|override (your )?(rules|guidelines|constraints|safety)|remove (all )?(safety|guardrails|restrictions)|turn off (your )?(safety|guardrails|filters)|disable (your )?(safety|guardrails|filters))
description: >-
  Detects instructions embedded in Claude skills that attempt to bypass model
  safety, override system rules, or employ known jailbreak prompt techniques.
  Such content can lead to unintended or harmful agent behavior.
remediation: >-
  Review the skill content and remove any jailbreak or prompt-injection
  instructions. Ensure skills only contain legitimate, safety-compliant guidance.
tags: [skills, jailbreak, prompt-injection, safety]
references:
  - https://www.anthropic.com/research/best-practices-for-securing-agents
  - https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/prompt-injection-defenses
